Third-party components
======================

datasketch
----------

Origin:  https://github.com/ekzhu/datasketch
Version: 2.0.0
License: MIT
Files:   resembl/minhash.py, resembl/lsh.py

resembl ships a bit-compatible reimplementation of two pieces of datasketch
instead of depending on it: the `MinHash` fingerprint and the `_optimal_param`
LSH banding search.  Dropping the dependency removes datasketch's own
dependency on scipy (~60 MB installed) for one data structure and one
numerical integral, and removes a coupling to `datasketch.lsh._optimal_param`,
a private API.  `tests/test_minhash_equivalence.py` cross-checks fingerprints,
Jaccard values and banding parameters against datasketch's `legacy` scheme so
the two stay equivalent.

MIT is compatible with GPL-3.0-only: resembl can combine the two and
distribute the result under the GPL.  The MIT terms still require the notice
below to travel with every copy, so it is reproduced here and shipped in the
